What:           /proc/qweovo_boot_status
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        QWEOVO kernel maintainer
Description:
                Public read-only boot decision, mode 0444. No write operation.
                Lines: schema_version=1, committed=0|1, sukisu=0|1,
                custom=0|1, status_spoofer=0|1, persistence=none, mutable=false.

                All features begin disabled. PID 1 may commit once using
                the private inherited anonymous decision FD. Other processes
                cannot commit, including children inheriting that FD. Closing
                its final reference without a valid choice seals all disabled.
                State is never persisted and cannot be changed after commit.

                /proc/qweovo_info also reports boot_policy and the currently
                available capabilities. Its stable identity remains readable
                with public controls disabled. CONFIG_QWEOVO_BOOT_MENU=n
                preserves the earlier always-available feature semantics.
